From: noti0na1 <noti0na1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 15:09:42 +0800
Subject: Add a mutable IdentitySet to optimize variable dependencies in CC
 (#26720)

`CaptureSet.Var.deps`, the set of capture sets that depend on a
capture-set variable, was a `SimpleIdentitySet`. Every `deps += cs`
therefore copied the whole element array. During capture checking of the
standard library, dependency sets grow to ~9,000 elements, it was the
single largest `Object[]` allocation site in the cc phase.

This PR replaces `deps` with a new `MutableIdentitySet`: a mutable,
insertion-order-preserving identity set. It is safe here because `deps`
already follows the "linear" discipline the data structure requires: the
previous value of `deps` is never used again after an update, only the
owning `Var` mutates it, and rollback operates through
`TypeComparer.logUndoAction` closures that act on the live object.

Unlike `EqHashSet`, iteration order is deterministic (insertion order
rather than hash-table order).

### 652-file stdlib: cc + setupCC

| run | baseline cc wall | PR cc wall | baseline cc allocated | PR cc
allocated |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| 1 | 5.39 s (20.6%) | 4.35 s (17.9%) | 2,622 MB (39.9%) | 1,789 MB
(31.1%) |
| 2 | 4.70 s (19.3%) | 4.45 s (17.3%) | 2,669 MB (40.3%) | 1,797 MB
(31.2%) |

